WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.726
GPU rental products differ in how much infrastructure the customer manages.

00:00:05.726 --> 00:00:13.284
Major cloud providers integrate GPU instances with mature identity, networking, storage, monitoring, and compliance services.

00:00:13.284 --> 00:00:19.468
Specialized GPU clouds may offer a wider accelerator selection or simpler pricing.

00:00:19.468 --> 00:00:30.232
Marketplace platforms can provide economical capacity from multiple hosts, but hardware consistency, trust boundaries, support, networking, and data-erasure assurances require careful review.

00:00:30.232 --> 00:00:37.790
Hosted notebooks are convenient for experiments and learning because an interactive environment can start quickly.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:45.349
They may have session limits, temporary storage, restricted networking, or less control over system packages.

00:00:45.349 --> 00:00:58.861
Dedicated instances provide an operating system and administrative control, making them suitable for custom environments and persistent services, but the renter owns patching, firewall rules, credentials, and shutdown.

00:00:58.861 --> 00:01:08.252
Serverless-style inference services hide much of the machine lifecycle and bill by request, execution time, or reserved endpoint capacity.

00:01:08.252 --> 00:01:19.016
They can reduce operations for supported models, though cold starts, model restrictions, data handling, and pricing at sustained volume must be evaluated.

00:01:19.016 --> 00:01:27.949
A managed endpoint and a raw GPU instance solve different problems even when both run the same model.

00:01:27.949 --> 00:01:30.468
On-demand pricing favors flexibility.

00:01:30.468 --> 00:01:36.194
Reserved or committed capacity can lower cost for predictable long-term use.

00:01:36.194 --> 00:01:46.042
Spot or interruptible capacity offers discounts because the provider may reclaim it, making it appropriate for restartable and checkpointed work.

00:01:46.042 --> 00:01:51.310
Also verify regions, quotas, minimum billing, support, and actual inventory.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:02:02.533
Select the service model that matches the job's duration, control needs, interruption tolerance, and data sensitivity, not simply the lowest advertised hourly rate.
